    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17592" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτ-ήκοος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκούω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who has himself heard, ear-witness,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐ. τινος γενέσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.133
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				658c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>hearing oneself,</i> i.e. <i>a law unto oneself,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.2
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>; so, <i>self-acquired,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρετή, ἐπιστήμη,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.371
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				354
			</span></i>.</div>
